A||N||4||DJWINNI||Where is the turn signals relay? NEED HELP!||||5||
Z||000000||DJWINNI||11-29-2001||05:23 PM||||Hi!<BR>My turn signals don't flash anymore and I would like to know where is the relay in order to replace it! Is it the same as the warning lights one? My warning lights flsh but my turn signals do not!<BR>Could you help me?||||reg||5
Z||000001||bocefas||11-29-2001||05:40 PM||||I think it's on the passenger side under the dash, right beside the blue box(your alarm chimes).  If it's not there, it's probably on the fuse block, I can't exactly remember where it is without looking.||||reg||1
Z||000002||DJWINNI||11-29-2001||05:42 PM||||Thanks for your answer Bocefas<BR>I know that the warning lights relay is located under the dash. Is it the same?||||reg||1
Z||000003||Voytek||11-29-2001||05:46 PM||||Actually, that's the emergency lights relay.<P>The turn signal relay is under the steering column.  It's a round little cylinder with (I believe) 2 wires on it.  It sits in a little metal bracket and you can just pop it out easily.  About $5 CDN bucks new.<P>Good luck.<BR><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/voyteks_sig2.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||bocefas||11-29-2001||05:54 PM||||He's right, my bad...I knew they weren't in the same place, but it's been like 2 years since I replaced mine, and you know the memory is the first thing to go...||||reg||1
